  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find the least natural number $n$ for which $\\frac{3060}{n}$ is a perfect square.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=85$.\n\nDivide by the largest square factor, $36$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3060&=2^2\\times3^2\\times5\\times17\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $\\frac{3060}{n}=k^2$, the least $n$ occurs when $k^2$ is the largest square factor of $3060$. Its prime exponents must be even, so $k^2=2^2\\times3^2=36$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=\\frac{3060}{36}\\\\n&=85\\\\\\frac{3060}{85}&=36=6^2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 56
  },
